    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "1SA9:1",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now there was a man of Benjamin, whose name was Kish the son of Abiel, the son of Zeror, the son of Becorath, the son of Aphiah, the son of a Benjamite, a mighty man of valor."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA9:3",
        "textualBasisJa": "The donkeys of Kish, Saul’s father, were lost. Kish said to Saul his son, “Now take one of the servants with you, and arise, go look for the donkeys.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA10:11",
        "textualBasisJa": "When all who knew him before saw that, behold, he prophesied with the prophets, then the people said to one another, “What is this that has come to the son of Kish? Is Saul also among the prophets?”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA10:21",
        "textualBasisJa": "He brought the tribe of Benjamin near by their families and the family of the Matrites was chosen. Then Saul the son of Kish was chosen; but when they looked for him, he could not be found."
      },
      {
        "ref": "1SA14:51",
        "textualBasisJa": "Kish was the father of Saul, and Ner the father of Abner was the son of Abiel."
      },
      {
